// Tutorial: SFZ Instruments (Experimental)
// Difficulty: intermediate | Duration: 5 min
// Description: Play multi-sampled instruments from .sfz files.

// SFZ is an open text format for sample-based instruments: it maps
// audio files across the keyboard so each note plays (and repitches)
// the nearest recording. Tons of free instruments exist in this
// format - pianos, strings, drums, and more.
//
// !! EXPERIMENTAL - KNOWN LIMITATION !!
// SFZ voices use MIDI-style NOTE_ON/NOTE_OFF, but melodies currently
// do NOT send NOTE_OFF. Consequences:
//   - Note lengths in your melody can't cut a note short: every
//     trigger plays its sample to the end, then releases on its own.
//   - Sustaining or looping SFZ patches (organs, pads, anything with
//     loop_mode=loop_continuous / loop_sustain) will hang and never
//     release. AVOID them.
// Stick to naturally-decaying instruments - plucks, pianos, drums,
// mallets - which auto-release when the sample finishes. That is
// what this tutorial uses.

set_tempo(90);

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 1: Load an SFZ instrument
// ------------------------------------------------------------
// load_sfz(id, path) parses the .sfz file and loads every sample
// it references (paths inside the .sfz resolve relative to the
// .sfz file itself).
//
// assets/tutorial_pluck.sfz is a minimal two-region instrument:
//
//   <group>
//   ampeg_attack=0.001
//   ampeg_release=0.15
//
//   <region>
//   sample=pluck_a3.wav      // recorded at A3...
//   pitch_keycenter=57       // ...so tell the player that
//   lokey=0
//   hikey=59                 // used for notes below C4
//
//   <region>
//   sample=pluck_a4.wav
//   pitch_keycenter=69       // recorded at A4
//   lokey=60
//   hikey=127                // used for C4 and above
//
// pitch_keycenter matters! It tells the engine what note the
// sample was recorded at, so other notes can be repitched from
// it. Without it, everything sounds out of tune.

let pluck = load_sfz("pluck", "assets/tutorial_pluck.sfz");

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 2: Put it on a voice
// ------------------------------------------------------------
// .on(sfz_handle) works exactly like .synth() - the voice now
// plays the SFZ instrument.

define_group("Plucks", || {
    let keys = voice("keys")
        .on(pluck)
        .gain(db(-6));

    // ------------------------------------------------------------
    // STEP 3: Play it
    // ------------------------------------------------------------
    // This melody crosses the C4 region split, so you hear both
    // samples being repitched - listen for the subtle timbre
    // change between the low and high halves.

    melody("keys_arp")
        .on(keys)
        .notes("A2 . C3 . E3 . A3 . | C4 . E4 . A4 . E4 .")
        .start();

    melody("keys_chords")
        .on(keys)
        .notes("[A2 E3 A3] - - - - - - - | [F2 C3 F3] - - - - - - -")
        .start();
});

// ============================================================
// WHERE TO GET INSTRUMENTS:
// Free SFZ libraries: VSCO 2 Community Edition (orchestral),
// Pianobook, sfz.org's instrument list. Remember the caveat at
// the top: prefer decaying instruments (piano, harp, mallets,
// drums) and avoid looped/sustaining patches for now.
//
// SUPPORTED OPCODES (the important ones):
//   sample            audio file for the region
//   lokey / hikey     key range that selects the region
//   lovel / hivel     velocity range (for velocity layers)
//   pitch_keycenter   the note the sample was recorded at
//   ampeg_attack / ampeg_decay / ampeg_sustain / ampeg_release
//                     amplitude envelope
//   volume / pan      per-region level and stereo position
//   seq_position / seq_length
//                     round-robin sample alternation
//
// TRY THIS:
// - Download a free SFZ piano and point load_sfz() at it
// - Add lovel/hivel regions to layer soft and hard samples
// - Change ampeg_release in the .sfz and reload
// ============================================================
